---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Main from "@/layouts/Main.astro";
import ProjectPreviewTitle from "@/components/ProjectPreviewTitle.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";
---

<Layout title={`Projects | ${SITE.title}`}>
  <Header />
  <Main
    pageTitle="Projects"
    pageDesc="A selection of projects I've built — spanning full-stack web apps, backend systems, and team collaborations."
  >
    <ul class="space-y-6">
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">CaseFlow Ops</h2>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-foreground/50">
          Individual backend project · In progress
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/80">
          A legal matter workflow platform for a small Australian law firm,
          developed with synthetic data. I am building the backend as a series
          of secure vertical slices, focusing on explicit access rules,
          transactional workflows, testable API contracts, and reproducible
          database evolution. The React frontend is not yet connected to the
          API, so the project is presented as backend work in progress.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-foreground/60">
          Java 21 · Spring Boot · Spring Security · JJWT · PostgreSQL · Flyway ·
          JUnit · MockMvc · Docker Compose · GitHub Actions
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Implemented</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-foreground/80">
            <li>
              Implemented BCrypt credential verification and stateless JWT
              authentication while reloading the current user from PostgreSQL on
              protected requests.
            </li>
            <li>
              Combined Partner, Lawyer, Paralegal, and Client roles with
              case-assignment and client-ownership checks at the service
              boundary.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built transactional Draft case creation with staff assignments and
              client creation with case-insensitive duplicate protection.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added explicit response models to keep persistence relationships
              and internal legal data out of API responses.
            </li>
            <li>
              Validated security and persistence behaviour with unit, MockMvc,
              and PostgreSQL integration tests.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added immutable Flyway migrations and GitHub Actions quality gates
              for backend tests and frontend lint/build checks.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/zxl3011/caseflow-ops"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            GitHub →
          </a>
          <span class="text-sm text-foreground/40">No live demo yet</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">
          Surfboard Rental Management System
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-foreground/50">
          Individual full-stack project
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/80">
          A full-stack rental management system covering booking, inventory
          management, and authentication workflows. I built the Spring Boot REST
          API using a layered backend structure, Dockerised the backend
          deployment, and deployed the frontend separately.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-foreground/60">
          Java · Spring Boot · REST APIs · Docker · Render · Vercel
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Highlights</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-foreground/80">
            <li>
              Designed backend API endpoints for rental and inventory workflows.
            </li>
            <li>
              Structured the backend using controller, service, and repository
              layers.
            </li>
            <li>Added validation and exception handling for API requests.</li>
            <li>
              Deployed the backend and frontend as separate application
              components.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 flex gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://surfboard-rental-management.vercel.app"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            Live Demo →
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/zxl3011/surfboard-rental-management"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            GitHub →
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
        <ProjectPreviewTitle
          headingLevel="h2"
          href="https://stitchflow-agent.crafty-cedar-1657.chatgpt.site/"
          imageAlt="StitchFlow project dashboard showing search, navigation, and a sample crochet workflow"
          imageSrc="/stitchflow-preview.jpg"
          title="StitchFlow"
        />
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-foreground/50">
          Individual full-stack product
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/80">
          An accessible workflow platform for knitters and crocheters working
          across complex patterns and inconsistent terminology. I evolved
          StitchFlow from a device-local prototype into an account-based product
          that securely synchronises structured projects, progress, images, and
          reusable measurement profiles across devices.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-foreground/60">
          TypeScript · React · Supabase Auth · PostgreSQL · Row-Level Security ·
          Cloud Storage · Cloudflare · Tailwind CSS
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Highlights</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-foreground/80">
            <li>
              Designed a typed Project, Section, Part, Row, Round, and Step
              domain model for editable craft workflows.
            </li>
            <li>
              Implemented stitch-level progress tracking with sequential
              completion inference and full manual override.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added email and Google authentication, PostgreSQL persistence,
              row-level access policies, and private image storage with
              Supabase.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built an explicit migration flow that lets existing users import
              local projects or retain their cloud data without silent
              overwrites.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added reusable measurement profiles, project search, client-side
              image optimisation, and cross-device synchronisation.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added reversible archiving, a Completed-project view, and
              confirmed permanent deletion of archived projects and their stored
              images.
            </li>
            <li>
              Simplified manual pattern entry with progressive disclosure and
              explicit flat, in-the-round, or unspecified construction methods.
            </li>
            <li>
              Delivered English and Simplified Chinese interfaces, US, UK, and
              Japanese terminology support, accessibility controls, and
              print-to-PDF output.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://stitchflow-agent.crafty-cedar-1657.chatgpt.site/"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            Live Demo →
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://youtu.be/x8B2VpBRKBw"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            Video Demo →
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Workforce Time Management System</h2>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-foreground/50">
          Team backend project · Code not public
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/80">
          A workforce management backend system built with Java Spring Boot and
          MySQL. The system supports staff administration, salary records,
          standard working hours, overtime rules, penalty configuration, and
          role-based access control data.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-foreground/60">
          Java · Spring Boot · MySQL · REST APIs · Azure DevOps · Postman
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">My Contributions</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-foreground/80">
            <li>Developed backend APIs for staff administration.</li>
            <li>
              Implemented salary history logic so new pay rates apply only to
              future records.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added support for staff standard working hours and validation
              rules.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built and collaborated on configuration APIs for overtime and
              penalty settings.
            </li>
            <li>
              Worked on role data and role endpoints to support authentication
              and access control.
            </li>
            <li>
              Tested backend endpoints with Postman and coordinated API
              contracts with frontend teammates.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Indigenous Art Atlas</h2>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-foreground/50">
          Team full-stack project · Code not public
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/80">
          An interactive web application for exploring Indigenous artworks on a
          map. The platform used Leaflet.js on the frontend and a PHP/MySQL
          backend to manage users, artwork data, artist profiles, collections,
          and access-controlled views.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-foreground/60">
          PHP · MySQL · JavaScript · Leaflet.js · Role-based access
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">My Contributions</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-foreground/80">
            <li>
              Implemented user registration, login, sessions, and role-based
              navigation.
            </li>
            <li>Built artist profile and artist application workflows.</li>
            <li>Developed user collection and favourite artwork features.</li>
            <li>Used prepared statements for safer database access.</li>
            <li>
              Integrated backend data with frontend pages and dynamic user
              views.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 flex gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://indigenous-art-atlas.onrender.com"
            class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            Live Demo →
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
